{
  "description": "Frozen vectors for the ATL Super-Tree: Data Tree roots as Super-Tree leaves, Super Roots, genesis_super_root, Super-Tree inclusion proofs and consistency-to-origin proofs. Derived from the ATL specification and the RFC 6962 algorithm text by an independent implementation, never by atl-core.",
  "provenance": {
    "super_leaves": "The eight Data Tree roots used as Super-Tree leaves are the published Certificate Transparency reference roots for tree sizes 1..8 (see test_data/vectors/merkle/trees.json, `roots`). Using published values as the leaves means the whole Super-Tree is anchored to externally known inputs.",
    "structure": "Derived from atl-protocol-ietf.md, 'Merkle Tree Structure' > 'Super-Tree (Global Chain Consistency)' and the 'Verification Algorithm' > 'Verify Super-Tree Proof' subsections, using the RFC 6962 Section 2.1 / 2.1.1 / 2.1.2 algorithms over an independent SHA-256."
  },
  "leaf_hashing_note": "A Data Tree root is used DIRECTLY as a Super-Tree leaf hash; it is NOT re-hashed as SHA256(0x00 || root_hash). The section 'Super-Tree Structure' only says the Super-Tree is \"a standard RFC 9162 Merkle Tree where each leaf is the root hash of a closed Data Tree\", which read literally would imply RFC 9162's own 0x00 leaf hashing on top. What settles it is the field definition of super_proof.genesis_super_root in 'Evidence Receipt (JSON)': \"The root hash of Super-Tree at size 1 (first Data Tree's root)\" -- a size-1 Merkle tree root equals its single leaf hash, so leaf hash == Data Tree root. These vectors follow that reading, which is also what atl-core implements. The prose in 'Super-Tree Structure' should be tightened, because an implementer reading only that section will compute a different Super Root.",
  "formulas": {
    "super_leaf": "SuperTreeLeaf[i] = DataTree[i].root_hash  (used as the leaf HASH, unhashed)",
    "super_root": "MTH over SuperTreeLeaf[0..super_tree_size), RFC 6962 Section 2.1 node rule",
    "genesis_super_root": "Super Root at super_tree_size == 1 == SuperTreeLeaf[0]",
    "inclusion": "PATH(data_tree_index, SuperTreeLeaf[0..super_tree_size)), RFC 6962 Section 2.1.1",
    "consistency_to_origin": "PROOF(1, SuperTreeLeaf[0..super_tree_size)), RFC 9162 Section 2.1.4 -- from_tree_size is always 1 per 'Consistency to Origin'"
  },
